{"connection_id": "BC-d918eba9b1fa5906b9da", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Tim.4.2", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "reproof with patience and instruction", "note": "The commentary makes counsel in truth and patience mutual duties; Paul directs Timothy to correct, rebuke, and encourage with complete patience and teaching."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ec3425089db24d3577cf", "ref": "SBLGNT:3John.1.5", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "faithful care for strangers", "note": "The commentary's asylum extends protection to an outsider; the elder praises work done faithfully for traveling brothers who were strangers to the host."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4c3276ba2b84da8e9dd5", "ref": "SBLGNT:3John.1.6", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "send travelers on their way", "note": "The commentary's quoted asylum includes bringing a protected outsider to a safe destination; the elder asks the host to send the travelers onward in a manner worthy of God."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c70297890717374d0517", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.12.10", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "iron prison gate opens for escape", "note": "The commentary's no-exit peril yields to rescue; Peter passes the guards and an iron gate opens of itself as he leaves confinement."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ae52a67158897c187a29", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.16.31", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "belief and household salvation", "note": "The commentary joins faith to an endangered person's family as a safe unit; Paul tells the jailer to believe in Jesus and promises salvation to him and his household."}
{"connection_id": "BC-788d2e0eb390a5d870c1", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.27.31", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "remain in ship to be saved", "note": "The commentary's false exit endangers a group; Paul says that unless the sailors stay in the ship, the others cannot be saved."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6254fc9dc201b360de23", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.27.32", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "cut away false escape boat", "note": "The commentary distinguishes holding to true rescue from a tempting wrong refuge; the soldiers cut the lifeboat's ropes after Paul's warning, keeping the endangered company together."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7b10d79af77f0f3755e2", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.27.44", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "whole company reaches land safe", "note": "The commentary reads its exception as escape and arrival; after remaining with the ship, every person in Paul's company reaches land safely."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ad706372e96785e14506", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.9.25", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "companions lower fugitive through wall", "note": "The commentary links rescue at an edge to a group standing with the endangered; Paul's disciples lower him in a basket through the city wall to escape a plot against his life."}
{"connection_id": "BC-da2575f73c2573e0a666", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.15", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "truth spoken in love sustains body", "note": "The commentary makes truth a guarded obligation and counsel reciprocal; Ephesians calls for speaking truth in love so the whole body grows into Christ."}
{"connection_id": "BC-342d31034d00c3f007fc", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.25", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "speak truth to one's neighbor", "note": "The commentary says people exhort one another in truth; Ephesians tells each person to put away falsehood and speak truth with a neighbor because they are members of one body."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8b469b6d04d7604ec16b", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.25", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "truth to neighbors as shared body", "note": "The commentary requires people to guard truth together; Paul commands each to speak truth to a neighbor because believers are members of one another."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ba429a92060c6995cea4", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.6.13", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "armor for evil day, stand firm", "note": "The commentary's armor protects amid an otherwise overwhelming calamity; Ephesians says to take full armor so the community can withstand the evil day."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6f6ed5497aa157ba9a8f", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.6.14", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "truth as protective armor", "note": "The commentary calls truth something to guard and mentions protective armor; Ephesians arms believers to stand with truth fastened as a belt."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b69bc1f0984616b67282", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.6.16", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "shield of faith", "note": "The commentary links iman with safety and armor with shelter; Ephesians calls faith a shield that extinguishes the evil one's arrows, making trust a protective defense."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cd7b3a168ed57244e547", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.6.16", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "faith as shield", "note": "The commentary makes faith an entry into security and uses armor as its image; Ephesians tells the group to take faith as a shield against burning attacks."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0cf6dff9a25cfb4fd0dd", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.6.17", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "helmet of salvation", "note": "The commentary names armor among the images of shelter; Ephesians specifically calls salvation a helmet, placing rescue within protective equipment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-71b0c9a17e27fa990274", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.6.17", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "salvation as helmet", "note": "The commentary's rescue has an armor image; Ephesians makes salvation the helmet of people standing in an evil day."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5f9a48842e47dac6a0ca", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.4.26", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Jerusalem above as mother", "note": "The commentary connects ancestral root and secure city; Paul calls the Jerusalem above free and the mother of believers, reworking lineage as civic belonging."}
{"connection_id": "BC-639e4103b06ec728cb39", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.2", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "bear one another's burdens", "note": "The commentary calls the sabīr one who stands with the group in its affairs; Paul tells believers to carry one another's burdens, describing that solidarity as fulfilling Christ's law."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7bdd0ec86de88a188824", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.2", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "bear one another's burdens", "note": "The commentary's sabir is a guarantor who stands with his people; believers are told to carry each other's burdens, making survival a shared obligation."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7fa0ec05c307ca32c642", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.9", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "do good without growing weary", "note": "The commentary names righteous deeds and patience together; Paul urges believers not to tire of doing good because they will reap at the proper time if they do not give up."}
{"connection_id": "BC-1591f03bd583ed0d2041", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.9", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "persist in good deeds until harvest", "note": "The commentary's saved group combines good acts with patience; Paul says not to grow weary in doing good because the harvest comes if they do not give up."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d449910ff755c5e768da", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.23", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "hold fast faithful promise", "note": "The commentary's grip becomes communal perseverance in faith; Hebrews commands holding fast the confession of hope because the promiser is faithful."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c9a54868d1d47bf7cf15", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.24", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "stir one another to love and good works", "note": "The commentary names mutual exhortation to righteous deeds; Hebrews tells believers to consider how to spur one another toward love and good works, giving the reciprocal practice a concrete form."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5890d7a5f5489bae2fcd", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.24", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "mutual encouragement to good deeds", "note": "The commentary's saved people do righteous acts and exhort each other; Hebrews urges mutual attention so love and good works increase."}
{"connection_id": "BC-249483f864d0afe0106c", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.25", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "encourage one another", "note": "The commentary says the group mutually exhorts one another; Hebrews commands encouragement as believers meet, especially as the day approaches, making support a shared practice."}
{"connection_id": "BC-75fc6af63ca1b4aa579a", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.25", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "gather and encourage under coming day", "note": "The commentary's sabir stands beside the group under danger; Hebrews commands continued assembly and reciprocal encouragement as the Day approaches."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3e55fe34cd7f5c244b38", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.36", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "endurance before receiving the promise", "note": "The commentary places a person in calamity and names patience among the saving qualities; Hebrews says believers need endurance to do God's will and receive what was promised."}
{"connection_id": "BC-893b95af52c9060cb7cc", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.36", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "endurance and doing God's will", "note": "The commentary joins patience to right action and deliverance; Hebrews says the hearers need endurance so that after doing God's will they receive the promise."}
{"connection_id": "BC-908e52e086629b7a356e", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.11.7", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "Noah's faith saves his household", "note": "The commentary's flood scene excludes Noah's son from the saved family; Hebrews says Noah built the ark by faith for the salvation of his household, a Christian account that includes the household in refuge."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e50e2f46dedf35771356", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.11.7", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "yorum_gelenegi", "basis": "Noah's faith builds family refuge", "note": "The commentary compares faith, deeds, and flood refuge; Hebrews interprets Noah's building of the ark for his household as obedient faith that condemns the world."}
{"connection_id": "BC-54ba8b8edfe697e4422f", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.12.22", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "arrival at the heavenly city", "note": "The commentary says the exception itself does not state arrival; Hebrews tells its hearers they have come to Mount Zion, the living God's city, making arrival at a secure city explicit."}
{"connection_id": "BC-241b7c3902e0dc12e999", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.12.22", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Mount Zion as heavenly city", "note": "The commentary contrasts a mountain trusted for safety with a safe city; Hebrews says its hearers have approached Mount Zion as the city of the living God."}
{"connection_id": "BC-bf99dbd51e227c7c26c4", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.13.14", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "seek the city to come", "note": "The commentary leaves the believers' destination unstated; Hebrews says Christians have no lasting city here but seek one to come, interpreting safety as future rather than present."}
{"connection_id": "BC-15fe70c64a0d0f8a46b7", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.13.2", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "hospitality to strangers", "note": "The commentary's quoted safe conduct for an outsider has a communal counterpart; Hebrews commands hospitality to strangers and recalls hosts who unknowingly welcomed angels."}
{"connection_id": "BC-bc0fa5eaaa2286b6e80b", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.3.13", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "exhort one another each day", "note": "The commentary's mutual exhortation guards the group; Hebrews says daily encouragement prevents anyone from being hardened by sin's deceit, explaining what the shared counsel protects against."}
{"connection_id": "BC-de60a3955d025b253a5a", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.3.13", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "exhort one another daily", "note": "The commentary emphasizes reciprocal advice in truth and patience; Hebrews commands daily mutual exhortation against the hardening caused by sin."}
{"connection_id": "BC-15c1cb13957f7808273a", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.4.16", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "approach the throne for help in need", "note": "The commentary calls asr a refuge for a person in distress; Hebrews invites people to approach the throne of grace to receive mercy and timely help, presenting access to God as refuge."}

item.stdout:
{"connection_id": "BC-ce68ace60400966851b1", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.4.16", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "approach sanctuary for timely help", "note": "The commentary reads safety as a place people may enter in need; Hebrews invites a confident approach to the throne of grace for mercy and help at the needed time."}
{"connection_id": "BC-942dd0a33a78d4f05e0f", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.6.18", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "flee for refuge and seize hope", "note": "The commentary describes a person clinging to shelter; Hebrews says those who fled for refuge take hold of the hope set before them, combining flight to safety with holding fast."}
{"connection_id": "BC-96ff370698bf1acd5c94", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.6.18", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "fled for refuge, grasp hope", "note": "The commentary's endangered person holds to a safe place; Hebrews says fugitives grasp the hope set before them as refuge."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3d36c0fc36165f452008", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.6.19", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "hope as an anchor", "note": "The commentary depicts a desperate person needing something to hold; Hebrews calls hope an anchor for the soul that reaches within the sanctuary, making inward security the image."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e92be67f42b231532e49", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.6.19", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "anchor enters inner sanctuary", "note": "The commentary connects holding fast with a secure destination; Hebrews makes hope an anchor of the soul that enters the sanctuary behind the curtain."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7b9b6612906f7f706a60", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.6.20", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "forerunner enters sanctuary for group", "note": "The commentary's sabir accompanies and guarantees the endangered; Hebrews presents Jesus as a forerunner who enters the inner sanctuary on the people's behalf."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c42b9c8d930b07ca85e9", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.7.22", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Jesus as covenant guarantor", "note": "The commentary's sabir is a guarantor who stays with the group; Hebrews explicitly makes Jesus the guarantor of a better covenant."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c308f34b1a40480203cb", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.7.25", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "intercessor saves those who approach", "note": "The commentary's communal guarantor accompanies people into security; Hebrews says Jesus lives to intercede and can save those who approach God through him."}
{"connection_id": "BC-1e361f46607e0dba9714", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jas.1.4", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "steadfastness leaves nothing lacking", "note": "The commentary develops sabr as endurance in calamity and khusr as loss; James says steadfastness must finish its work so believers become complete, lacking nothing."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7f2fd384242383b413b6", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jas.2.17", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "faith without deeds dead", "note": "The commentary's safe exception includes both faith and righteous works; James argues faith without works is dead, sharpening that pairing."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ea68af984f0d858304e3", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jas.2.22", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "faith active with works", "note": "The commentary lists belief and righteous deeds together; James says Abraham's faith was working with his works and was brought to completion by them, offering an explicit interpretation of their relation."}
{"connection_id": "BC-34ed35ca9efd0c0b1805", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jas.2.22", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "faith completed in deeds", "note": "The commentary binds belief to practiced good; James uses Abraham to say faith worked with his actions and was brought to completion by them."}
{"connection_id": "BC-27ae139b491108920b87", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jas.5.11", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Job's endurance and the Lord's compassion", "note": "The commentary associates sabr with enduring calamity; James blesses those who endure and points to Job and the Lord's compassionate outcome, preserving both suffering and rescue."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cc3cfb5a2629f240635a", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jas.5.19", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "turn back a wanderer from truth", "note": "The commentary calls truth something one protects for another; James addresses anyone who restores a person straying from truth."}
{"connection_id": "BC-33340a725b31ddb42a5b", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jas.5.20", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "rescuer saves soul from death", "note": "The commentary's communal guarantor prevents another's ruin; James says bringing back the wanderer saves a soul from death."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e87c0276caf658a307e1", "ref": "SBLGNT:John.10.11", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "true shepherd stays and dies", "note": "The commentary's communal guarantor remains with those in peril; Jesus calls himself the good shepherd who lays down his life for the sheep."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f945d02cae29f81d1727", "ref": "SBLGNT:John.10.12", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "hired guard deserts flock", "note": "The commentary's sabir stays beside the group in danger; the hired worker flees the wolf, leaving the flock exposed."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6a7ebb56f172f7e583da", "ref": "SBLGNT:John.10.28", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "no one snatches the sheep from Jesus' hand", "note": "The commentary identifies believers with those who entered safety; Jesus promises his sheep eternal life and says no one can snatch them from his hand, making security explicit."}
{"connection_id": "BC-557ede620d7fe8f30b4f", "ref": "SBLGNT:John.10.28", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "no one snatches from hand", "note": "The commentary's grip and secure dwelling oppose destruction; Jesus promises his sheep will never perish or be snatched from his hand."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a50b86cac1fd101f324e", "ref": "SBLGNT:John.10.9", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "enter gate, be saved", "note": "The commentary imagines the exception as crossing into a safe place; Jesus calls himself a gate through which entrants are saved and find pasture."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6b97444f66db0bd5da03", "ref": "SBLGNT:John.3.16", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "belief prevents perishing", "note": "The commentary's exception moves believers out of destructive loss; Jesus' saying promises that whoever believes will not perish but have life."}
{"connection_id": "BC-1da568e6d1f357fb982e", "ref": "SBLGNT:John.5.24", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "belief crosses death to life", "note": "The commentary reads faith as entry into safety; Jesus says a hearer who believes has already passed from death to life and avoids judgment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-54f841c40805313ff9ee", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jude.1.23", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "snatch others out of fire", "note": "The commentary pictures people at the edge of destruction needing communal rescue; Jude commands others to be saved by being snatched from fire."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d1753c1e183fc9162db5", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jude.1.3", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "contend for the delivered faith", "note": "The commentary calls truth something to be guarded; Jude urges believers to contend for the faith once delivered to the saints, giving that protection a communal action."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f734ed0e850bb7e3cd67", "ref": "SBLGNT:Luke.10.34", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "stranger moves injured man to shelter", "note": "The commentary's sabir stays with the endangered and helps him reach safety; the Samaritan binds the wounded stranger, carries him to an inn, and cares for him."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6395143dfbb37f7d1600", "ref": "SBLGNT:Luke.10.35", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "stranger guarantees continuing care", "note": "The commentary defines sabir as one who guarantees a community member's welfare; the Samaritan pays the innkeeper and promises to repay further costs."}
{"connection_id": "BC-37aecd7d06028470383c", "ref": "SBLGNT:Luke.12.18", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "larger barns as planned refuge", "note": "The commentary's false shelter can be constructed; the rich man plans bigger barns for his surplus immediately before learning his life is demanded."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5ea7a90502cddf713f19", "ref": "SBLGNT:Luke.12.19", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "wealth imagined as secure rest", "note": "The commentary says a shelter may be false; the rich man tells himself his stored goods guarantee many years of ease."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4d06322218756d64b526", "ref": "SBLGNT:Luke.12.20", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "sudden death undoes false security", "note": "The commentary names loss as destruction and warns against a false refuge; God demands the rich man's life that night despite his storage plan."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4cd17a99210349fc34db", "ref": "SBLGNT:Luke.15.20", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "father receives lost son at home", "note": "The commentary makes ancestry and home a place of return from loss; the father runs to embrace the returning son while he is still far off."}
{"connection_id": "BC-383095847561c8a18111", "ref": "SBLGNT:Luke.15.24", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "lost and dead son found alive", "note": "The commentary uses loss for destruction and a familial refuge for escape; the father describes the restored son as formerly dead and lost but now alive and found."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e2bb2a0185f4d10afe85", "ref": "SBLGNT:Luke.21.16", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "kin hand disciples to death", "note": "The commentary includes lineage as a possible refuge; Jesus says even parents, siblings, relatives, and friends will betray disciples, so kinship cannot guarantee safety."}
{"connection_id": "BC-eaaaa800910dc1c8dffa", "ref": "SBLGNT:Luke.21.19", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "endurance gains life", "note": "The commentary connects sabr with danger and loss; Jesus tells disciples facing persecution that by endurance they will gain their lives, making perseverance a path through peril."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6b98b019b47cb0eb5141", "ref": "SBLGNT:Luke.21.19", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "endurance gains life", "note": "The commentary places patience after danger and loss; Jesus tells threatened disciples they will gain their lives by endurance."}
