{"connection_id": "BC-d2f0b8da46a2e720997c", "ref": "Babylonian Talmud, Sotah 37a", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "yorum_gelenegi", "basis": "Nahshon enters the sea first", "note": "The commentary describes a no-exit peril and rescue through trust; the rabbinic account has Nahshon step into the sea before it parts, reading deliverance as requiring a first act of communal faith."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c350536d0d5f4554584e", "ref": "Bava Kamma 60a", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "yorum_gelenegi", "basis": "stay indoors during destruction", "note": "The commentary's secure home answers a calamity with no safe exit; this discussion reads the Passover order not to leave home as instruction to remain inside while destruction moves outside."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8ecca29ee4344ac7df73", "ref": "Genesis Rabbah 32:6", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "yorum_gelenegi", "basis": "Noah delays entering the ark", "note": "The commentary identifies believers with those who enter safety; a midrash commonly located at Genesis Rabbah 32:6 portrays Noah as hesitating until the waters press him into the ark, complicating that entry with a reading of delayed trust (the locator is from memory)."}
{"connection_id": "BC-13048524d4227c5d43f7", "ref": "Makkot 10a", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "yorum_gelenegi", "basis": "marked roads to refuge cities", "note": "The commentary's shelter is a place an endangered person must reach; this rabbinic discussion requires roads and signs guiding a fugitive toward the cities of refuge."}
{"connection_id": "BC-bd9494763c3a7b4c21ea", "ref": "Mishnah Makkot 2:5", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "yorum_gelenegi", "basis": "escorts for fugitive to refuge", "note": "The commentary's sabir accompanies the endangered to safety; the Mishnah sends two learned escorts with a killer fleeing toward a refuge city so the avenger does not kill him on the way."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b2cdb2aa90a46cbc5521", "ref": "Mishnah Makkot 2:6", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "yorum_gelenegi", "basis": "refuge residents supplied by priestly mothers", "note": "The commentary's guarantor helps a trapped community endure; this Mishnah says mothers of high priests gave food and clothing to exiles in refuge cities so the exiles would not pray for their sons' deaths."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c321d93b66e642455832", "ref": "Shabbat 54b", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "yorum_gelenegi", "basis": "failure to protest communal wrongdoing", "note": "The commentary's truth must be protected through mutual counsel; this discussion holds a person answerable for wrongdoing within a household or community if able to protest and silent."}
