{"connection_id": "BC-740a46c119374e5c7aa9", "ref": "WLC:Ezek.13.11", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "failed wall in destructive storm", "note": "The commentary warns against false shelter; the prophet says the whitewashed wall promising peace will fall under flood and storm."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e789ac57be85628d8624", "ref": "WLC:Ezek.14.14", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "karsi_anlati", "basis": "Noah delivers only himself", "note": "The commentary's Noah scene includes a son who cannot shelter himself by lineage; Ezekiel names Noah among the righteous who could save only their own lives in a judged land, limiting the refuge righteousness provides."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e8e036715518eb1f7c89", "ref": "WLC:Ezek.14.20", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "karsi_anlati", "basis": "sons and daughters not delivered", "note": "The commentary notes lineage as a possible refuge but recounts Noah's son perishing; Ezekiel explicitly says even Noah could not deliver sons or daughters, making kinship no guarantee against judgment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-bcfc711c316a30b8c925", "ref": "WLC:Ezek.22.30", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "stand in breach for community", "note": "The commentary's sabir stands with and guarantees a group; God seeks someone to stand in the wall's breach on the land's behalf to avert destruction and finds no one."}
{"connection_id": "BC-af45f073c7c9b9eb7fa9", "ref": "WLC:Ezek.33.6", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "watchman obliged to warn", "note": "The commentary says truth is something a person must protect and commends mutual exhortation; a watchman who fails to warn of the sword bears responsibility for a neighbor's blood."}
