{"connection_id": "BC-57ad5b2f2a317f46aba0", "ref": "WLC:Josh.2.19", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "inside house versus outside death", "note": "The commentary imagines an exception from destruction as arrival in safety; Rahab's rescuers make the house boundary decisive for her relatives' survival."}

